    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d328-a4">

                <pb facs="0767" n="671" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg671"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1879-07-09"><hi rendition="#small-caps">July</hi> 9,
                        1879</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I beg to state that I have been informed by
                    the authorities that in consequence of the spread of cholera now prevalent in
                    various localities from Kioto and Ozaka to <pb facs="0768" n="672"
                        xml:id="pg672"/> the Shiga, Gifu, and Miye prefectures, orders have been
                    sent that travelers coming to Tokei by land will be detained at points on the
                    main lines of communication in the Yamanashi and Gumba prefectures, and at
                    Mishima, in the Shidzuoka prefecture, during five days from the day of their
                    arrival before being allowed to pass on.</p>
                <p>I take, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>TERASHIMA MUNENORI</signed>, [<hi rendition="#small-caps">l.
                        s.</hi>]<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Minister for Foreign
                    Affairs</hi>.</closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His Excellency Sir <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harry S. Parkes</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
